{
  "case_id": "2017-17-333",
  "document_hash": "d0dc013999b70159252824ed3dab9324a50dcd9d96ce76d6ec724cb3759c2288",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0dc013999b70159252824ed3dab9324a50dcd9d96ce76d6ec724cb3759c2288",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0dc013999b7-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:03 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Appellants",
      "case_id": "2017-17-333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0dc013999b70159252824ed3dab9324a50dcd9d96ce76d6ec724cb3759c2288",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0dc013999b7-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All nine justices in Vieth against Jubelirer agreed that partisan gerrymandering can violate the Constitution. The principal question presented in this case is whether this Court has the Article III authority to do anything about it. We submit that it does under the First Amendment. According to this Court's First Amendment retaliation and ballot access cases, government officials may not single out particular individuals for disfavored treatment on the basis of the views that they have expressed at the ballot box in prior elections."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-17-333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0dc013999b70159252824ed3dab9324a50dcd9d96ce76d6ec724cb3759c2288",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0dc013999b7-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Do you see the applicability of any other test? You have a lot of amici with different tests, the ACLU."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kimberly",
      "case_id": "2017-17-333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0dc013999b70159252824ed3dab9324a50dcd9d96ce76d6ec724cb3759c2288",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0dc013999b7-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KIMBERLY: Well, we -- there are two reasons. It was our understanding when we filed the amended complaint back in 2015 that we would not have made out a claim under a number of those other tests, and we were concerned because the focus here really was on the Sixth District and not the map as a whole, that it just wasn't an apt way of thinking about what happened in Maryland."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-17-333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0dc013999b70159252824ed3dab9324a50dcd9d96ce76d6ec724cb3759c2288",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0dc013999b7-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What do you -- what do you think would be permissible? You -- you said your theory allows for de minimis exceptions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kimberly",
      "case_id": "2017-17-333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0dc013999b70159252824ed3dab9324a50dcd9d96ce76d6ec724cb3759c2288",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0dc013999b7-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KIMBERLY: Well, I think a good example would be -- as I was just describing to Justice Sotomayor, it would be what happened in the Eighth Congressional District."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-17-333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0dc013999b70159252824ed3dab9324a50dcd9d96ce76d6ec724cb3759c2288",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0dc013999b7-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Counsel, one question I have about causation for you."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kimberly",
      "case_id": "2017-17-333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0dc013999b70159252824ed3dab9324a50dcd9d96ce76d6ec724cb3759c2288",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0dc013999b7-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We have evidence uncontested in this case that those metrics are reliable ways of predicting electoral outcomes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-17-333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0dc013999b70159252824ed3dab9324a50dcd9d96ce76d6ec724cb3759c2288",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0dc013999b7-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Suppose the Maryland Constitution had a provision that required that partisan advantage for one party be the predominant consideration in any districting. Lawful or not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-17-333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0dc013999b70159252824ed3dab9324a50dcd9d96ce76d6ec724cb3759c2288",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0dc013999b7-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Along the lines of things we don't know, we've been talking about the intent of the legislature, but what effect does the -- does the fact that this map was subsequently approved by the people themselves have when we're trying to determine intent?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-17-333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0dc013999b70159252824ed3dab9324a50dcd9d96ce76d6ec724cb3759c2288",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0dc013999b7-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: -- and passed with 64 or so percent of the vote."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Sullivan",
      "case_id": "2017-17-333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0dc013999b70159252824ed3dab9324a50dcd9d96ce76d6ec724cb3759c2288",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0dc013999b7-0002-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SULLIVAN: Yes, it did."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Sullivan",
      "case_id": "2017-17-333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0dc013999b70159252824ed3dab9324a50dcd9d96ce76d6ec724cb3759c2288",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0dc013999b7-0002-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SULLIVAN: Well, if independent voters had support of that Democratic candidate on the merits of that candidate because they thought that candidate was the better candidate, as happened in the Sixth District when independent voters voted very heavily for the Democratic candidate, then you would be harming them if you were -- if you were -- I don't know if you were going to think about"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Sullivan",
      "case_id": "2017-17-333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0dc013999b70159252824ed3dab9324a50dcd9d96ce76d6ec724cb3759c2288",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0dc013999b7-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SULLIVAN: No. When you get to the end of the process, there needs to be a showing of totality of circumstances with historical and sociological evidence of exclusion of that minority, which simply is not the case when you're talking about Republicans. They have -- they're a major party. They've been in control of government oftentimes, and as they are now."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-17-333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0dc013999b70159252824ed3dab9324a50dcd9d96ce76d6ec724cb3759c2288",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0dc013999b7-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Is there anything"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Michael B. Kimberly",
      "case_id": "2017-17-333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0dc013999b70159252824ed3dab9324a50dcd9d96ce76d6ec724cb3759c2288",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0dc013999b7-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position is that the -- the burden properly understood under the First Amendment and applied in this context is the same burden that this Court has recognized in the ballot access cases. It's -- it's making it more difficult -- deliberately making it more difficult for particular citizens to achieve electoral success because their views are disapproved by those in power, in this case, in Annapolis."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Michael B. Kimberly",
      "case_id": "2017-17-333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0dc013999b70159252824ed3dab9324a50dcd9d96ce76d6ec724cb3759c2288",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0dc013999b7-0003-0003",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And I guess what I would say is if that -- if that approach isn't going -- is -\u00ad is going to work in any case, it's going to work in this one because, here, the evidence is unequivocal that this was the intent. And, point in fact, the political composition of the district turned 180 degrees. It went from Republican to Democrat, just as the map drawers intended."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-17-333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "d0dc013999b70159252824ed3dab9324a50dcd9d96ce76d6ec724cb3759c2288",
      "evidence_id": "ev-d0dc013999b7-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 11:06 a.m., the hearing adjourned.)"
    },
    {
